# Commit each function

After a function or feature is complete, create a git commit for that slice before starting the next one.

- One concern per commit (homepage, login, routing, a panel, a bugfix).
- Do not batch unrelated functions into a single commit.
- Follow the repo git protocol: never update git config, never skip hooks, never force-push, commit only when the user wants commits. This project wants a commit per function by default.
- Stage only the files for that function.
- Use a short message that says why the slice exists.
